3. She finds the idea of wearing children's clothing from Walmart’s junior section impractical and confusing. (Verbatim: "i'm totally gonna fit in the clothes for a nine year old... it'll be adorable yeah")  
4. She values comfort in clothing over strict fashion rules. (Verbatim: "personally when it comes to like fashion just wear what you're comfortable in to be honest")  
5. She believes comfort contributes to happiness and a positive appearance. (Verbatim: "comfy things make me happy and then if i'm happy i'll probably look better as a happier person")  
6. She has experienced discomfort from wearing ill-fitting clothes in the past. (Verbatim: "i was down i'm down to wear like i don't mean t-shirts but why do they want me to go to the junior section")  
